## Prerequisites

- Go {{GO_VERSION}}+
- Docker and docker-compose (for local development stack)
- Make

## Quickstart

```bash
# Copy environment config
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env as needed (see Configuration below)

# Start local dev stack (database + app)
make compose-up

# Run database migrations (SQL databases only)
make migrate-up

# Run the server
make run

# Open Swagger UI
open http://localhost:8080/docs/
```

## Common Commands

| Command              | Description                                    |
|----------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| `make run`           | Run the server with `.env` loaded              |
| `make build`         | Build the server binary into `bin/`            |
| `make build-cli`     | Build the CLI binary (if configured)           |
| `make build-all`     | Build both server and CLI                      |
| `make test`          | Run unit tests with race detector              |
| `make test-integration` | Run integration tests (requires Docker)     |
| `make lint`          | Run golangci-lint                              |
| `make swagger`       | Regenerate OpenAPI spec from annotations       |
| `make compose-up`    | Start local dev stack                          |
| `make compose-down`  | Stop local dev stack                           |
| `make migrate-up`    | Run database migrations up                     |
| `make migrate-down`  | Roll back one migration                        |
| `make migrate-create`| Create a new migration file                    |
| `make cover`         | Generate coverage report                       |
| `make install-hooks` | Install the pre-commit git hook                |
| `make ci`            | Run all checks (vet, lint, swagger, test)      |

## Project Structure

```
cmd/
  server/          Server entry point
internal/
  adapters/
    http/          HTTP handlers, middleware, routing
    store/         Database adapters (memory, SQL, or MongoDB)
    telemetry/     OpenTelemetry and structured logging
  config/          Configuration loading and validation
  core/            Business logic (services)
  auth/            JWT/OAuth authentication middleware
pkg/
  domain/          Domain types, ports (interfaces), errors
deploy/            Dockerfile, docker-compose
migrations/        SQL migration files (if applicable)
docs/              Architecture docs, OpenAPI spec
```

## Configuration

Configuration is loaded from environment variables. See `.env.example`
for all available settings with documentation.

Key settings:

| Variable         | Description                          | Default   |
|------------------|--------------------------------------|-----------|
| `HTTP_PORT`      | Server listen port                   | `8080`    |
| `LOG_LEVEL`      | `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`     | `info`    |
| `AUTH_ENABLED`    | Enable/disable JWT authentication   | `true`    |
| `DATABASE_URL`   | Database connection string           | —         |

## API Documentation

When the server is running, interactive API documentation is available at:

    http://localhost:8080/docs/

The OpenAPI spec is generated from handler annotations using
[swag](https://github.com/swaggo/swag). Regenerate after changing
handler annotations:

```bash
make swagger
```

## Authentication

JWT/OAuth token validation is built in. Configure via environment:

- Set `AUTH_ENABLED=false` to disable during development
- Set `AUTH_JWKS_URL` for RS256/ES256 (JWKS auto-refresh)
- Set `AUTH_HMAC_SECRET` for HS256

See `.env.example` for all auth settings.

